
# Supabase project credentials. Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the
# values from your Supabase project settings (Project Settings > API).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Not needed yet — no real production domain has been chosen for this
# project (see src/app/robots.ts and src/lib/site-url.ts's doc comments).
# Set this to the real https:// origin once one is, so page metadata
# (src/app/layout.tsx's metadataBase) and email links sent with no request
# Origin header (src/lib/email/notification-triggers.ts) point at it
# instead of the placeholder default.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Signup confirmation emails are sent by Supabase Auth itself (supabase.auth.signUp
# in src/lib/supabase/auth-actions.ts) — there is no env var here for that, and
# adding one would do nothing. Supabase's own default mailer is shared and rate-
# limited (a few emails/hour) and is meant for local development only; if
# confirmation emails aren't arriving in production, configure a real provider in
# the Supabase Dashboard under Authentication > SMTP Settings (enable "Custom
# SMTP"), and confirm Authentication > URL Configuration lists this app's actual
# Site URL and /auth/callback redirect URLs for every environment. None of that is
# configurable from this repo.

# Required for: the two cron endpoints (src/app/api/cron/*, via
# src/lib/email/notification-events.ts and createServiceRoleClient), the
# admin dashboard's total-user count, and the payment code
# (src/app/api/billing/webhook/[provider]/route.ts, src/lib/billing/payments). Bypasses Row Level Security
# entirely — server-only, never exposed to the client, never prefixed
# NEXT_PUBLIC_. From Project Settings > API > service_role secret.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Wayl (https://thewayl.com) — one-time payments, charged in IQD. Premium is
# priced in USD in this app (per plan and country tier, see
# src/lib/billing/plans.ts) and converted to IQD at a fixed rate (see
# src/lib/billing/pricing.ts) on the server immediately before each payment
# link is created; the link carries currency=usd so Wayl's page shows dollars.
# The Wayl API this integration is built on has no recurring/subscription
# endpoints, so every payment grants one fixed period of premium (the chosen
# plan's days) and nothing renews automatically.
# All three variables below are server-only — never exposed to
# the client, never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_. Leave any unset to keep the honest
# "not connected" behavior (checkout shows "Billing isn't connected yet", the
# webhook route responds 501). Payments also need SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# (above) and CRON_SECRET (below, for the payments-reconcile job).
#
# WAYL_API_KEY: from the Wayl merchant dashboard (API Platform > Manage Keys).
# The same key is used for test and live links.
# WAYL_API_KEY=
#
# A long random value YOU generate (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`; at least 16
# characters here, Wayl accepts 10-255). It is sent to Wayl with every payment
# link and used to verify the x-wayl-signature-256 signature of every webhook.
# WAYL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
#
# "test" creates test-mode links (Wayl's `env: "test"` on the same API, with the
# same key); "live" creates real, charged links and is only honored in a
# production build, so a developer machine can never create real payment links.
# Must be set explicitly — there is no default. Never set "test" on a deployment
# real visitors use: a test-mode payment still grants real premium here.
# WAYL_ENV=
#
# Optional. By default Wayl's payment page is asked to show the price in dollars
# (the payment link carries currency=usd), converted by Wayl at its own rate; the
# charge itself is always in dinars. Set to "false" to leave Wayl's page showing
# dinars instead, for example while Wayl's dollar rate and ours (pricing.ts)
# differ. A change needs a new deploy to take effect.
# WAYL_SHOW_USD=
#
# Wayl calls back <NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL>/api/billing/webhook/wayl and sends the
# learner back to <NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL>/billing/return. When testing on a
# Netlify deploy preview or branch deploy, set NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL for that
# deploy context to that deploy's own URL, so both reach it instead of production.

# Optional. Comma-separated sign-in emails exempt from the sitewide free-access
# promotion (Admin > Free access), so the paid flow can be tried end to end on a
# tester's own account while everyone else keeps the promotion: for those accounts
# the price and checkout button show, and only a purchase makes them Premium. It
# can only ever remove access, never grant it. Case doesn't matter; a change needs
# a new deploy to take effect.
# FREE_ACCESS_EXCLUDED_EMAILS=

# Resend API key (server-only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_). Once this and
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS are both set, src/lib/email/provider-registry.ts starts
# returning a real Resend-backed adapter and real emails go out for welcome,
# milestone, and inactive-learner-reminder messages. Leave both unset to keep
# emails logged-only ("queued") instead of actually sent — e.g. in local dev.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# The "from" address Resend sends as — must be on a domain verified in the
# Resend dashboard (Domains > Add Domain, then the DNS records it gives you).
# Either a bare address ("noreply@yourdomain.com") or "Name <address>".
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=

# Optional. Where a learner's reply goes when they answer an email from us
# (including the support emails an admin sends from Admin > Users, Reports or
# Inbox). To read those replies inside the app (Admin > Inbox), set this to an
# address on your Resend RECEIVING domain and finish the EMAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# setup below. Or set it to any mailbox you already read (Gmail, Zoho, …) and
# skip the Inbox. Leave unset to have replies go to EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS.
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO_ADDRESS=

# Admin > Inbox: replies arrive through a Resend webhook. One-time setup:
#   1. Resend dashboard > Domains > (your domain) > enable Receiving, and add
#      the MX record it shows. If the domain already has MX records for a
#      mailbox (Google Workspace, Zoho…), use a SUBDOMAIN for receiving
#      (e.g. reply.yourdomain.com) so you don't take over your existing mail.
#   2. Set EMAIL_REPLY_TO_ADDRESS (above) to an address there, e.g.
#      support@reply.yourdomain.com.
#   3. Resend dashboard > Webhooks > Add Webhook: URL
#      https://<your-site>/api/email/inbound, event "email.received".
#   4. Copy that webhook's Signing Secret ("whsec_…") here.
# The route reads the message body with EMAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY, so that key
# must be allowed to read received emails (use a Full access key if a
# sending-only key gets a 401/403). Also needs SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY and
# the 20250326000000_inbound_emails.sql migration applied. Until this is set
# the webhook answers 501 and nothing is stored.
# EMAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Not needed yet — the AI translation pipeline (see the multilingual-
# content-architecture Phase 3 work) has no provider connected until this is
# set. Once it is, src/lib/translation/provider-registry.ts starts returning
# a real Anthropic-backed provider and the admin "Generate translation"
# action becomes usable. Server-only: never exposed to the client, never
# prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Which Claude model the translation pipeline calls
# (src/lib/translation/anthropic-provider.ts) — defaults to Claude Sonnet 5
# if unset.
# TRANSLATION_MODEL=

# Nothing to configure for narration to work at all: with none of the
# variables below set, src/lib/voice/provider-registry.ts automatically uses
# Edge-TTS (Microsoft Edge's built-in Read Aloud neural voices) — free, no
# API key, no account, no signup, works immediately. Set up an Edge-TTS
# voice in Admin > Voice > "Edge-TTS voices" ("Add suggested voices" seeds
# several real voices in one click) and pick a "Default narration voice" in
# the Narration settings card below it. The variables below are entirely
# optional upgrades, tried in this order (ElevenLabs, then Cartesia, then
# Hume AI, then Edge-TTS), each falling back to the next if
# unset/unavailable:

# ElevenLabs — the original (paid) expressive-narration provider. Covers
# Stories, Conversation lessons, and Books. Server-only: never exposed to
# the client, never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Cartesia — a paid expressive-narration provider, used only when
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY above is NOT set. Get a key at https://play.cartesia.ai
# (Settings > API Keys). In this app: Admin > Voice > "Cartesia voices" —
# search Cartesia's catalog and add the ones you want (or paste a voice id
# directly), then set the Model field in the Narration settings card to a
# Cartesia model id (e.g. "sonic-2") and pick a default narration voice.
# Server-only: never exposed to the client, never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# CARTESIA_API_KEY=

# Hume AI — a paid expressive-narration provider, used only when none of the
# providers above are set. Get a key at https://app.hume.ai/keys. In this
# app: Admin > Voice > "Hume AI voices" — browse Hume's Voice Library and add
# the ones you want (or paste a voice id directly), then pick a default
# narration voice in the Narration settings card. Server-only: never exposed
# to the client, never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# HUME_API_KEY=

# Which Claude model the Voice Director (src/lib/voice/director.ts) calls to
# turn a story's sentences into per-sentence delivery direction — defaults
# to Claude Sonnet 5 (same tier as TRANSLATION_MODEL) if unset.
# VOICE_DIRECTOR_MODEL=

# Required for all four cron endpoints (src/app/api/cron/inactive-learners,
# src/app/api/cron/translation-sweep, src/app/api/cron/voice-sweep, and
# src/app/api/cron/kokoro-voice-sweep) to run at all: a long random value
# shared between the scheduler and this app, checked as
# `Authorization: Bearer <value>` (both GET, for a platform scheduler, and
# POST, for a manual/other caller). Without it, every one of these endpoints
# always responds 501 and never runs. If deploying to Vercel with the
# vercel.json crons in this repo, set this as a Vercel project env var —
# Vercel automatically sends it as that same `Authorization: Bearer` header
# on every cron-triggered request, so no other wiring is needed.
# Generate with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# CRON_SECRET=

# Web Push (VAPID) — browser push notifications (src/lib/push), sent with
# the standard Web Push API, no third-party push service or account needed.
# Once both are set, the "Enable notifications" toggle in Settings works and
# src/app/api/cron/inactive-learners-push starts actually sending pushes
# instead of no-op'ing. Leave both unset to keep the toggle showing "not
# available on this deployment" instead of erroring.
# Generate a pair with `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys` — free, one command,
# no dashboard/account. The public key is safe to ship to the browser (that's
# what NEXT_PUBLIC_ means here); the private key must stay server-only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Optional — the "contact us" identity sent with every push request per the
# Web Push spec (mailto: or https:). Falls back to deriving one from
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS above, then to a generic default, so this rarely needs
# to be set explicitly.
# VAPID_SUBJECT=

# Cloudflare Turnstile — bot protection on the sign-up form (see
# register-form.tsx and src/lib/turnstile/verify.ts). Free, no card
# required. Leave both unset to keep sign-up exactly as it was before this
# was added (no CAPTCHA shown, no server-side check run).
#
# To get these two values at no cost:
#   1. Go to https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/turnstile and sign in
#      (a free Cloudflare account is enough — no domain/DNS setup needed).
#   2. Add a site: any name, add this app's real domain (and "localhost" for
#      local development), widget mode "Managed".
#   3. Copy the Site Key into NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY (safe to expose
#      to the client — it's meant to be public) and the Secret Key into
#      TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY (server-only, never expose this one).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# The optional post-lesson "rate the app" prompt (RatingPrompt) — sends each
# submission to a Google Sheet via a Google Apps Script Web App, kept
# entirely outside Supabase on purpose so non-technical admins can browse
# and chart it directly. Leave both unset to keep the prompt logging to the
# console in development and silently doing nothing in production (never
# blocks or errors the lesson-completion screen either way).
#
# To set this up for free: create a Google Sheet, add a header row
# (Timestamp, Rating, Comment, LessonId, Mode, Locale, UserType, AnonId),
# then Extensions > Apps Script and paste a doPost(e) handler that checks
# `body.secret` against RATINGS_WEBHOOK_SECRET below and appends a row.
# Deploy it (Deploy > New deployment > Web app, Execute as: Me, Who has
# access: Anyone) and copy the resulting /exec URL below. Both are
# server-only — never exposed to the client, never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# RATINGS_WEBHOOK_URL=
# RATINGS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Optional. The real average rating and number of ratings, shown as one line on
# /upgrade ("4.8 average from 120+ ratings"). Ratings live in the Google Sheet
# above, not in the database, so copy the two figures from it by hand (for
# example =AVERAGE(B:B) and =COUNT(B:B) over the Rating column). They must be the
# real figures. Nothing is shown until both are set, the average is between 1 and
# 5 and there are at least 20 ratings; the average is rounded down to one decimal
# and the count is rounded down. A change needs a new deploy to take effect.
# SOCIAL_PROOF_RATING=
# SOCIAL_PROOF_RATING_COUNT=

# Sentry — production error monitoring (see sentry.client.config.ts,
# sentry.server.config.ts, sentry.edge.config.ts). Free tier: 5,000
# errors/month, no card required. Leave unset to keep today's behavior
# (errors only visible via console.error/server logs, nothing tracked).
#
# To get this at no cost:
#   1. Create a free account at https://sentry.io/signup/.
#   2. Create a project: platform "Next.js".
#   3. Project Settings > Client Keys (DSN) — copy the DSN value below.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
#
# Optional: lets Sentry upload readable stack traces (source maps) instead
# of minified ones, and needs an auth token from
# https://sentry.io/settings/account/api/auth-tokens/ (scope: project:releases).
# Safe to leave unset — builds still work, error reports are just harder to
# read.
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
